input.text:
**Code Change Description:**
The changes were driven by the need to align the Spring AI Mistral integration with the latest capabilities of the Mistral AI platform. Specifically: 1) The original `ChatCompletionMessage` content handling was insufficient for complex responses involving citations and 'thinking' traces, necessitating a more robust, chunk-based structure. 2) To provide parity with recent model advancements, the client needed explicit support for 'reasoning' parameters (`ReasoningEffort`) and metadata extraction for citation/reference features. 3) The refactoring of the API client and internal model logic ensures better adherence to evolving JSON schema requirements and provides a cleaner interface for users to access advanced model features.
This update significantly enhances the `spring-ai-mistral-ai` library to support advanced Mistral AI features, including 'thinking' models, citations/references, and structured content handling. Key changes include: 1) Updating `ChatCompletionMessage` to handle complex, multi-type content chunks (text, images, references, and thinking content) via custom Jackson serialization/deserialization. 2) Introducing `ReasoningEffort` and updating `MistralAiChatOptions` to support the new reasoning capabilities. 3) Adding new metadata keys (`reference_content`, `reference_thinking_content`, `thinking_content`) to `MistralAiChatModel` to extract and propagate model-generated insights and references into the response metadata. 4) Refactoring `MistralAiApi` to replace the deprecated `ChatCompletionFinishReason` with a more generic `FinishReason` and updating request object construction to support modern API parameters. 5) Adding extensive new integration tests and infrastructure (`ThinkingModelUtils`, `ThinkingModelSource`) to verify citation and reasoning capabilities.

